sub:assertion {
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/morphoeval-delphi10000-aulacopleura-koninckii-holaspis18-turing-wavelength-s0> a pk:Claim ;
        rdfs:label "Turing wavenumber at 15.49 µm on Aulacopleura koninckii holaspis18 (428.3 Ma) faithfully reproduces Aulacopleura koninckii_holaspis18 morphology" ;
        dct:description "The simulation script(s) models/2026-delphi10000-aulacopleura-koninckii-holaspis18-turing-wavelength-s0.py implement the cited source model as published and produce forms that match real Aulacopleura koninckii_holaspis18 specimens and the source authors' figures. A belief under audit, not a fact: its credibility is carried by the MorphoEval rubric assessments." ;
        dct:subject <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/models/2026-delphi10000-aulacopleura-koninckii-holaspis18-turing-wavelength-s0.py> ;
        pk:context "script(s): https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/models/2026-delphi10000-aulacopleura-koninckii-holaspis18-turing-wavelength-s0.py; output: docs/media/aulacopleura_koninckii_holaspis18_turing_wavelength_s0_comparison.png; organism: Aulacopleura koninckii_holaspis18; environment: n/a; claim_boundary: [reported_in_source: Hughes & Chapman 1995 and Fusco et al. 2004: meraspid segment addition and a variable holaspid thoracic number, including 18 segments. | Fusco, Hong & Hughes 2016: axial growth gradients along the trunk. | Turing 1952: reaction-diffusion selects a finite critical wavelength. | Commons File:Aulacopleura konincki.jpg, 14 mm, Silurian, CC BY-SA 3.0.; reconstructed_in_script: Jacobian and D_v/D_u = 40 solved so lambda_c = 15.49 µm = 1.549e-05 m at 428.3 Ma. | Rib-span fraction 0.2245 on the pinned photograph, applied to the meraspis (4.2 mm, 12 segments, 428.5 Ma) and holaspis22 (22 mm, 22 segments, 428.1 Ma) lengths. | Mode counts 5, 11 and 14. Midline rib Pearson r = 0.9832; lateral transect Pearson r = 0.9863. | Cuticle mask from red-minus-green chroma, 70th percentile, largest component.; transfer_boundary: species_gallery meraspis / holaspis18 / holaspis22 JPEGs are byte-identical, so only the Commons photograph is an independent image. | The photograph resolves pleural ribs at hundreds of micrometres. The 15.49 µm wavelength is the cellular-scale law, not a feature counted on the photograph.; does_not_claim: Does not claim a published holochroal lens diameter of 15.49 µm for this species. | Does not claim a second assessor. | Does not claim the chroma mask is a histological outline of the pleurae.]; phenomenon_size: 11 µm (1.088e-05 m, log10=-4.963 m, tier=4_cellular_10um); species_scale_ladder (10 runs from 11 µm to 2.4 cm): 11 µm:aulacopleura-koninckii-holaspis18-bioelectric-polarity, 34 µm:aulacopleura-koninckii-holaspis18-vertex-packing, 544 µm:aulacopleura-koninckii-holaspis18-turing-wavelength, 1.1 mm:aulacopleura-koninckii-holaspis18-clock-wavefront, 2.4 mm:aulacopleura-koninckii-holaspis18-morphogen-condensation, 3.0 mm:aulacopleura-koninckii-holaspis18-elastic-buckling, 3.4 mm:aulacopleura-koninckii-holaspis18-flux-canalization, 4.8 mm:aulacopleura-koninckii-holaspis18-branching-tree" ;
        pk:derivedFromPaper <https://doi.org/10.1016/0022-5193(79)90042-0>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1017/pab.2016.5>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1086/381042>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1098/rstb.1952.0012>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1111/j.1502-3931.1995.tb01824.x> .
    <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/models/2026-delphi10000-aulacopleura-koninckii-holaspis18-turing-wavelength-s0.py> a schema:SoftwareSourceCode ;
        rdfs:label "models/2026-delphi10000-aulacopleura-koninckii-holaspis18-turing-wavelength-s0.py" ;
        schema:codeRepository <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib> ;
        schema:programmingLanguage "Python" .
}

sub:provenance {
    sub:assertion prov:wasAttributedTo <https://orcid.org/0000-0000-0000-0000> ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://doi.org/10.1016/0022-5193(79)90042-0>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1017/pab.2016.5>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1086/381042>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1098/rstb.1952.0012>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1111/j.1502-3931.1995.tb01824.x> .
    <https://doi.org/10.1016/0022-5193(79)90042-0> dct:title "Simple chemical reaction systems with limit cycle behaviour" .
    <https://doi.org/10.1017/pab.2016.5> dct:title "Axial growth gradients across the postprotaspid ontogeny of the Silurian trilobite Aulacopleura koninckii" .
    <https://doi.org/10.1086/381042> dct:title "Exploring developmental modes in a fossil arthropod: growth and trunk segmentation of the trilobite Aulacopleura konincki" .
    <https://doi.org/10.1098/rstb.1952.0012> dct:title "The chemical basis of morphogenesis" .
    <https://doi.org/10.1111/j.1502-3931.1995.tb01824.x> dct:title "Growth and variation in the Silurian proetide trilobite Aulacopleura konincki" .
}

